<title>FRANCE: Eiffage sells Portugal motorways stake.</title>
<headline>Eiffage sells Portugal motorways stake.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-01-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>French public works group Eiffage said on Friday it recently sold a 10 percent stake in Portuguese motorways firm BRISA to two bodies controlled by the Portuguese state.</p>
<p>The sale to state entities IPE and CGD was for an undisclosed sum.</p>
<p>Eiffage said in a statement that the sale, as well as other previous operations it did not identify, brought the company half way towards achieving a one-billion-franc target for disposals, announced in September. It said the disposal plan was going forward in &quot;satisfactory conditions and in accordance with the company's programme.&quot;</p>
</text>
